{"type": "message", "message": "**Minimalist means keeping what makes your home work—and reducing visual clutter.** It doesn’t mean an empty room or everything painted white.\n\nFor your small flat, that could mean:\n- **A complete, restrained seating area:** comfortable seating, a reachable table, a rug and a lamp—not lots of scattered little pieces.\n- **Useful closed storage:** everyday belongings have a home without filling every surface.\n- **A simple palette:** warm off-white, wood and one accent colour, with texture to keep it welcoming.\n- **Clear routes:** arrange furniture so the bedroom, windows and balcony doors remain easy to reach.\n\nThe aim is **less competing for attention, not less comfort**. These are design ideas only; nothing has been changed.", "conversationId": "8c9c19a0aa3642e0bbfc9136f271fbf6"}
